{"strongs": "H0898", "word": "בָּגַד", "translit": "ba.gad", "root": "אתת", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "act or deal treacherously", "definition": "[ בָּגַד ] verb act or deal treacherously — Qal Perfect בָּֽגְדָה Jer 3:20 + 14 t.; Imperfect יִבְגֹּד Mal 2:15 + 5 t.; נִבְגַּד Mal 2:10 Infinitive absolute בָּגוֺד Isa 48:8 ; Jer 5:11 construct בְּגֹד Isa 33:1 בִּגְדוֺ Exod 21:8 Participle בֹּגֵד Prov 22:12 + 11 t.; בּוֺגֵד Isa 33:1 + 10 t.; — act or deal treacherously, faithlessly, deceitfully , in the marriage relation, in matters of property or right, in covenants, in word and in general conduct. \\ \\ a. absolute 1Sam 14:33 ; Job 6:15 ; Ps 78:57 ; Isa 24:16 ; Isa 33:1 (twice in verse); Isa 48:8 ; Mal 2:11 . compare phrases אחי בגדו כמו נחל my brethren have dealt deceitfully as a brook Job 6:15 בֹּגְדִים בָּנָ֑דוּ וּבֶגֶד בּוֺגְדִים בָּגָ֑דוּ the treacherous have dealt treacherously, yea in treachery have the treacherous dealt treacherously Isa 24:16 (striking alliteration); בֹּגְדֵי אָוֶן treacherous in wickedness Ps 59:6 . \\ \\ b. with בְּ Exod 21:8 ( E ), Judg 9:23 ; Isa 33:1 (twice in verse); Jer 3:20 ; Jer 5:11 ; Jer 12:6 ; Lam 1:2 ; Hos 5:7 ; Hos 6:7 ; Mal 2:10 ; Mal 2:14 ; Mal 2:15 ; Mal 2:16 . \\ \\ c. with accusative Ps 73:15 . \\ \\ d. with מִן pregnant, בָּֽגְדָה אִשָּׁה מֵרֵעָהּ acteth treacherously (in departing) from her friend Jer 3:20 . The participle is used Prov 2:22 + 8 t., Ps 25:3 ; Ps 59:6 ; Ps 119:158 ; Isa 21:2 ; Isa 24:16 (twice in verse); Isa 33:1 ; Jer 3:8 ; Jer 3:11 ; Jer 9:1 ; Hab 1:13 ; Hab 2:5 בֹּגְדֵי בָ֑גֶד dealers treacherously in treachery (very treacherously ) Jer 12:1 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB901')\">BDB901</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H898')\">H898</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB900')\">BDB900</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB902')\">BDB902</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>בָּגַד</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>act or deal treachero